// Desktop tools you download. A new save starts with none: each is a file on a board (an item
// `Tool(id)` in a board's FILES), and once you own one it's on your desktop for good.
//   id     what boards and the save call it
//   name   what the desktop and the Shell call it
//   blurb  one line for the board's listing
//   intro  the cracktro it opens with every time (an id in data/intros/), or leave it out
// What each one unlocks is the game's (hub::Save::has_tool):
//   wardial  the `wardial` Shell command and CarrierTerm's WarDial tab
//   hexed    the HexEd tool at home, and `hex`, patch and optimize in a run
//   qwkread  the QWK mail reader at home: bulletins and saved textfiles from your boards
//   icedb    the ICE database at home: every ICE you've fought, and what breaks it
//   nightcomm the hacker's dashboard at home: heat on every number, a wardialer that replaces
//             wardial's tab, the ranges you know and the watched lines you've found
[
    (id: "wardial", name: "WarDial", blurb: "A demon dialer: scans a block of numbers for carriers.", intro: Some("wardial")),
    (id: "hexed",   name: "HexEd",   blurb: "A hex editor for warez binaries. Patch, optimize, break things.", intro: Some("hexed")),
    (id: "icedb",   name: "ICE DB",  blurb: "A bestiary of intrusion countermeasures. Fills in as you meet them.", intro: Some("icedb")),
    (id: "nightcomm", name: "NiGHTCOMM", blurb: "A hacker's dashboard: heat on your numbers, a wardialer, ranges and watched lines.", intro: Some("nightcomm")),
    (id: "qwkread", name: "QWK Reader", blurb: "Offline mail: read your boards' bulletins and saved textfiles at home.", intro: Some("qwkread")),
]
